            "text": "```python\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\ndef business_days(date1, date2):\n    d1 = datetime.strptime(date1, \"%Y-%m-%d\").date()\n    d2 = datetime.strptime(date2, \"%Y-%m-%d\").date()\n\n    # Make the calculation work regardless of date order\n    if d1 > d2:\n        d1, d2 = d2, d1\n\n    count = 0\n    current = d1 + timedelta(days=1)\n\n    while current < d2:\n        if current.weekday() < 5:  # Monday=0 through Friday=4\n            count += 1\n        current += timedelta(days=1)\n\n    return count\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```python\nprint(business_days(\"2024-01-01\", \"2024-01-08\"))\n# 4\n```"
